### 8.1 Universal Output Contract Rules

- Every artifact must have an owner, creation phase, source-of-truth basis, source trace, decision status, and completion criteria.
- Every registry artifact must support completeness checks, duplicate checks, orphan checks, unmapped checks, contradiction checks, and handoff-integrity checks.
- Every CSV registry must use canonical IDs, not presentation labels, as primary keys.
- Every non-trivial artifact must include explicit blocker handling and exact downstream handoff.
- No artifact passes because it has a file name. It passes only when the schema is complete and proof checks pass.

### 8.2 Decision Vocabulary

| Decision | Meaning | When Lawful |
|---|---|---|
| `Keep` | Retain as an active canonical item. | Target-fit item passes review cleanly. |
| `Merge` | Combine multiple donor items into one canonical item. | Multiple donor fragments serve one clean canonical intent. |
| `Convert` | Change unit type or structural form. | A screen should become a sheet, modal, section, or state-only unit. |
| `Internal` | Retain as internal support unit only. | Not a user-facing screen but still operationally necessary. |
| `Move to Legacy` | Remove from live clean tree and isolate. | Not active in current clean execution model. |
| `REFERENCE_ONLY` | Use as evidence only, not as a clean repo item. | Donor material informs but does not transfer. |
| `REBUILD_CLEAN` | Re-implement from clean law. | Default when bulk donor carryover is unfit or risky. |
| `EXTRACT_PARTIAL` | Carry over only a well-bounded fragment. | Fragment is proven target-fit and safe to extract. |

