### 10.1 Universal Gate Formula

- Required artifacts: exact named artifacts for the phase.
- Required evidence: evidence index or phase evidence folder proving the current claim.
- Pass conditions: completeness + coherence + explicit proof checks + blocker classification + handoff readiness.
- Fail conditions: missing artifact, placeholder-only artifact, contradiction, unresolved duplicate/orphan/unmapped drift, or fake completion claim.
- Recovery conditions: repair only the failing checks; do not widen scope during gate recovery.
- Blocker escalation: if the blocker cannot be resolved within phase law, mark `BLOCKED` and stop progression.

## 11. Proof Law, Evidence Law, and Runtime Proof Ladder

### 11.1 Evidence Law

- Canonical evidence root: `kdt/volatile/registry/runs/{SESSION_ID}/`.
- Every serious operation, extraction, rebuild, gate, and closure claim must be evidence-backed.
- No phase passes on file existence alone.
- No artifact passes because it has a name.
- No sign-off without explicit evidence index.
- No closure claim without counts, completeness checks, duplicate checks, orphan checks, unmapped checks, contradiction checks, donor-coverage checks, and handoff-integrity checks.

### 11.2 Runtime Proof Ladder

| Class | Meaning | Allowed Claim | Forbidden Claim |
|---|---|---|---|
| Shell readiness | Folder/project shell exists. | Scaffold exists. | Flow works. |
| Registry-only preview | Registries and specs exist. | Truth is documented. | UI works or binding works. |
| Visual-only preview | Layout and CTA review only. | Visual review possible. | Runtime proof or production-like proof. |
| Limited-API preview | Targeted contract/screen validation only. | Specific API assumption validated. | Canonical truth or full propagation proof. |
| Canonical local truth | Bound path uses explicit runtime truth source. | Bound local truth path exists. | Production-like proof for untested scope. |
| Production-like proof | Required surfaces, propagation, persistence, and health explicitly verified. | Tested proof scope works. | Untested flows also work. |
| Packaging build | App/package can be packaged. | Package compiles/builds. | Runtime truth or functional proof. |

## 12. Final Close Law and Appendices

### 12.1 Final Close Law

- No package, service, phase, or artifact may claim final closure until structure integrity, reference integrity, placeholder elimination, artifact reality, donor coverage, screen completeness, operation completeness, grouping completeness, handoff integrity, contradiction absence, and implementation readiness all pass.
- Only two final outcomes exist: `FINAL_CLOSE = PASS` or `FINAL_CLOSE = FAIL`.
- There is no “mostly complete,” “good progress,” or “close enough” final state.
- Any unresolved closure ambiguity must be `BLOCKED`, `GAP`, or `UNPROVEN`.

### 12.2 Forbidden Patterns

- Blind donor carryover.
- API-first rebuild.
- Binding-first rebuild.
- Runtime-first rebuild.
- Preview used as proof.
- File existence used as proof.
- Unresolved placeholders in active packs.
- Broken references in active packs.
- Donor naming leakage into canonical truth.
- Service truth hidden in shells.
- Business logic inside UI Kit.
- Raw fetch on canonical bound paths.
- Control-panel as ownership trash can.
- Silent gaps, silent blockers, or silent contradictions.

### 12.3 Status Vocabulary

| Status | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `BLOCKED` | Cannot proceed lawfully until blocker is resolved or explicitly superseded. |
| `GAP` | Known deficiency exists and must be closed before the relevant claim can pass. |
| `UNPROVEN` | Claim is not yet evidence-backed. |
| `RESOLVED` | Issue was closed lawfully with evidence. |

### 12.4 One-Line Operating Rule

Build the clean repo from clean law, real donor recovery, real registries, real evidence, and real closure. Do not confuse a better-written package with a sealed execution package.
